SDL 3.4.16, pinned for Zimbr

Upstream: https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/tree/release-3.4.16
Archive: https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/archive/refs/tags/release-3.4.16.tar.gz
Archive SHA-256: c2ee715e42ec520c4d11fd8d249ef1d2b2baf4ad31148b72b3b000276c0b3633
Zig package hash: N-V-__8AABHq9wIiTHGY4qR6mw45F_TX8FSvqsQQ-Wtq1tzY

This directory retains provenance and SDL's license. build.zig.zon pins the
upstream archive; Zig downloads and verifies it as a lazy dependency. The full
upstream archive lives in the dependency cache, outside the tracked source tree.
Zimbr builds the library directly through build/sdl.zig with Zig 0.16.0.

Local C changes are recorded in build/sdl/vulkan.patch and confined to
src/render/vulkan/SDL_render_vulkan.c:
- Reuse completed staging allocations with a bounded upload-buffer pool.
- Preserve shared vertices and submit indexed geometry.
- Reuse constant-buffer contents and matching descriptor sets within a command list.

The build invokes GNU patch with --batch, --forward, and --fuzz=0. Both the
original renderer and patch are tracked build inputs. The patched renderer is a
declared output in the build cache; the upstream dependency is never modified.
An unsuccessful patch application stops the build before compiling SDL.
The source list excludes the original renderer so only the generated copy is
compiled. Includes resolve against the pinned upstream tree.

These are Zimbr modifications, not an unmodified upstream SDL release. The
benchmark's SDL revision includes a SHA-256 prefix covering the upstream package
hash followed by the patch bytes. Cached builds skip unchanged patch preparation.

The Linux configuration and explicit source/protocol lists are in build/sdl/.
They enable Wayland, offscreen/dummy video, Vulkan, OpenGL, GLES2, SDL GPU,
software rendering, Fcitx through D-Bus, compositor text input, and libdecor.
The direct IBus backend is enabled when pkg-config finds ibus-1.0. Use -Dibus=false
to disable it or -Dibus=true to require its development files. Optional audio and
device integrations use development headers discovered by pkg-config; their
runtime libraries are loaded by SDL. The application requires no installed SDL.
Wayland bindings are generated from the pinned XML by wayland-scanner as Zig
build steps. Graphics loaders, drivers, and other OS services remain external.

To update SDL, update the URL and content hash in build.zig.zon, rebase the
renderer patch against that release, and reconcile build/sdl/sources.zig and
build/sdl/SDL_build_config.h with that release's CMake source lists/configuration.
Update this provenance, the version macros in build/sdl.zig, and the revision
prefix. Generate the unified diff from pristine and edited copies of the renderer,
using a/src/render/vulkan/SDL_render_vulkan.c and
b/src/render/vulkan/SDL_render_vulkan.c as its labels. Verify that applying it
reproduces the edited file exactly and that the pristine copy stays unchanged.
Run both renderer test suites, real IME scenarios, and rendering benchmarks.

The upstream SDL license and embedded third-party notices are preserved. Binary
packages include SDL's license, HIDAPI's original permissive license, and the
BSD license for yuv2rgb alongside Zimbr's notices.
